/-!
# Constructing the solvable factors in 13.6.13

The literal X-family now lies in the faithful offender actor on U_v, with
normality, solvability, two-perfectness and its Thompson commutator intact.
The source-correct B.5.6 application retains every nontrivial alternative.

The single-S₃ alternative now constructs every field of
`NormalS3Decomposition`, including the literal Thompson equality and the
marked product maps. The two-factor and hyperplane alternatives, and the
exclusion of the quasisimple and outer alternatives, remain to be proved.
In particular the outer A₆–C₃ alternative cannot be discarded merely
because X is solvable. Those branches must use the earlier marked A₅
configuration; this module does not assert the full 13.6.13.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, printed p.929.
-/
